# Loaded only for `vite dev` / dev-mode builds, never for a production build.
# Production leaves this unset and falls back to window.location.origin —
# the SPA and API are genuinely same-origin there (ADR-0005). In dev, the SPA
# and API run as separate processes on separate ports, so this points
# directly at the real API port; the backend's dev-only CORS policy
# (Program.cs) allows this SPA origin to reach it.
#
# Must match launchSettings.json's "https" profile — specifically the
# 8081 port it shares with the Docker profile's ASPNETCORE_HTTPS_PORTS,
# not the 7214 port also listed there (a leftover scaffold-generated
# port). https, not http: OpenIddict's self-hosted server derives its
# discovery document's issuer/endpoint URIs from its own bound address,
# so authority has to match the scheme the API is actually serving on.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://localhost:8081
